; majalops.com — Cloudflare DNS import
;
; Paste into Cloudflare: DNS > Records > Import and Export > Import.
; Cloudflare manages SOA and NS itself and ignores them here, so they are
; deliberately absent.
;
; ORIGIN_IP is 203.0.113.10 throughout. That address is from the range RFC 5737
; reserves for documentation: it is guaranteed not to route anywhere, so an
; unfinished import cannot quietly point a live name at somebody else's server.
; Replace every occurrence before importing:
;
;     sed -i 's/203\.0\.113\.10/YOUR.SERVER.IP/g' majalops.com.zone
;
; TTL is 300 while the migration settles. Raise it to 3600 once the addresses
; have stopped moving — a five-minute TTL is a nuisance to nobody but is the
; difference between a ten-minute and a one-hour fix when something is wrong.

$TTL 300

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The site
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

; Apex. Proxy this one (orange cloud) — it is the only way to get a redirect
; rule from majalops.com to www without running a server for it.
@                       300     IN  A       203.0.113.10

www                     300     IN  CNAME   majalops.com.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The application
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

; The Odoo demo, served by deploy/demo (Caddy on 80/443 in front of Odoo on
; 8069). Set DEMO_HOST=demo.majalops.com in that stack's .env.
;
; Import this DNS-only (grey cloud) and leave it that way until Caddy has
; issued its certificate: the HTTP-01 challenge is far less trouble when the
; request reaches your server rather than Cloudflare's edge. Switch to proxied
; afterwards, and only with SSL/TLS mode set to Full (strict) — Flexible puts
; Cloudflare on HTTPS and your origin on HTTP, which Caddy answers with a
; redirect to HTTPS, and the two loop until the browser gives up.
demo                    300     IN  A       203.0.113.10

; Odoo's API is not a separate service — XML-RPC and JSON-RPC answer on the
; same host as the application. This name is therefore an alias, not a tier,
; and it exists so the address can be published now and moved later without
; reprinting anything. If a real gateway ever appears, repoint it here.
api                     300     IN  CNAME   demo.majalops.com.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Placeholders — these resolve nowhere until the service behind them exists
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

; Cloudflare Pages, built from construction-erp/docs/. Replace with the
; <project>.pages.dev hostname Pages gives you, then add the custom domain on
; the Pages side; it will verify against this record.
docs                    300     IN  CNAME   majalops-docs.pages.dev.

; Status page. Every provider (Better Stack, Instatus, Statuspage) hands you a
; hostname to point at, and every one of them requires the record to be
; DNS-only — a proxied status page is a status page that goes down with the
; thing it reports on.
status                  300     IN  CNAME   status-provider.example.net.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Mail — the domain sends no email, and says so
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; A new domain with no SPF and no DMARC is a free From: address for anybody who
; wants one, and a Majal invoice is a plausible thing to forge. These two
; records say the domain sends nothing and that anything claiming otherwise
; should be rejected outright.
;
; The moment you add real email (Google Workspace, Zoho, Cloudflare Email
; Routing), both of these must change or your own mail will be binned. There is
; no MX record here for the same reason: adding one blindly during a migration
; is how mail silently stops.

@                       300     IN  TXT     "v=spf1 -all"
_dmarc                  300     IN  TXT     "v=DMARC1; p=reject; rua=mailto:dmarc@majalops.com"
